1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,707
A new checkout feature is ready to ship on Friday.

2
00:00:03,707 --> 00:00:04,926
The total is wrong,

3
00:00:04,926 --> 00:00:06,850
a test fails only on weekends,

4
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:10,377
and nothing stops a bad change from reaching customers.

5
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,109
Can you make this code trustworthy?

6
00:00:13,109 --> 00:00:13,856
Not by hope.

7
00:00:13,856 --> 00:00:15,851
With tests that catch real bugs,

8
00:00:15,851 --> 00:00:17,097
a gate that says no,

9
00:00:17,097 --> 00:00:18,842
and a report that proves it.

10
00:00:19,392 --> 00:00:22,243
This is the software testing mastery lesson.

11
00:00:22,243 --> 00:00:23,409
One real scenario,

12
00:00:23,409 --> 00:00:25,935
every skill from the last nine lessons,

13
00:00:25,935 --> 00:00:28,203
and a judge that checks six things.

14
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:31,014
Find it. Fix it. Gate it. Prove it.

15
00:00:32,564 --> 00:00:35,636
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

16
00:00:36,186 --> 00:00:40,282
One: a look back at the whole domain, eight objectives, in one picture.

17
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:45,205
Two: the mastery scenario. Five missions, in a fixed order, and a judge.

18
00:00:45,755 --> 00:00:50,235
Three: a live worked example of the whole scenario, with real pytest.

19
00:00:50,785 --> 00:00:51,997
Four: your own run,

20
00:00:51,997 --> 00:00:53,337
judged by six checks,

21
00:00:53,337 --> 00:00:56,143
with a report that documents what you found.

22
00:00:56,143 --> 00:00:57,036
Then clean up.

23
00:00:57,586 --> 00:01:01,426
This is lesson ten, the last lesson of the software testing domain.

24
00:01:01,976 --> 00:01:04,237
Find it. Fix it. Gate it. Prove it.

25
00:01:06,287 --> 00:01:10,575
First, the map of the domain. Eight objectives, and you have done every one.

26
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:16,010
Test types: unit, integration, API, end to end, smoke, and regression.

27
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:21,936
Assertions, fixtures, mocks, and isolation: small tests that fail for one reason.

28
00:01:22,486 --> 00:01:24,486
Running tests and reading reports,

29
00:01:24,486 --> 00:01:25,722
including exit codes,

30
00:01:25,722 --> 00:01:28,310
and the browser tests with the trace viewer.

31
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:32,935
API and health tests: check the running service, not just the code.

32
00:01:33,485 --> 00:01:38,413
Coverage: find the code nobody tests, and remember that coverage is not quality.

33
00:01:38,963 --> 00:01:43,870
Tests in CI: a gate that says no, with a coverage floor and required checks.

34
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:48,900
Performance and security tests: a time budget, and a scan for secrets.

35
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:52,799
And flaky tests: find the cause, and never just rerun.

36
00:01:53,349 --> 00:01:55,973
Today, they all work together in one scenario.

37
00:01:57,523 --> 00:02:00,616
Five missions, and then the judge. Do them in this order.

38
00:02:01,166 --> 00:02:03,005
Mission one: find the bug.

39
00:02:03,005 --> 00:02:03,994
Run the tests.

40
00:02:03,994 --> 00:02:05,974
One fails for a real reason.

41
00:02:05,974 --> 00:02:07,247
The test is right,

42
00:02:07,247 --> 00:02:08,802
and the code is wrong.

43
00:02:08,802 --> 00:02:09,721
Fix the code.

44
00:02:10,271 --> 00:02:12,302
Mission two: fix the flaky test.

45
00:02:12,302 --> 00:02:13,699
It passes on weekdays,

46
00:02:13,699 --> 00:02:15,095
and fails on weekends.

47
00:02:15,095 --> 00:02:16,238
Pass a fixed date,

48
00:02:16,238 --> 00:02:18,079
instead of reading the clock.

49
00:02:18,629 --> 00:02:20,524
Mission three: cover the code.

50
00:02:20,524 --> 00:02:21,156
Add tests,

51
00:02:21,156 --> 00:02:23,999
until the coverage is ninety percent or more.

52
00:02:23,999 --> 00:02:26,969
Test the edges: five thousand is free shipping,

53
00:02:26,969 --> 00:02:30,128
and four thousand nine hundred ninety-nine is not.

54
00:02:30,678 --> 00:02:32,553
Mission four: write the gate.

55
00:02:32,553 --> 00:02:35,204
A CI script that fails when a test fails,

56
00:02:35,204 --> 00:02:37,338
when coverage drops under ninety,

57
00:02:37,338 --> 00:02:39,019
or when a secret is found.

58
00:02:39,569 --> 00:02:41,483
Mission five: write the report.

59
00:02:41,483 --> 00:02:42,718
Four lines: the bug,

60
00:02:42,718 --> 00:02:43,706
the flaky cause,

61
00:02:43,706 --> 00:02:44,508
the coverage,

62
00:02:44,508 --> 00:02:45,990
and the number of tests.

63
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:50,999
That report is your evidence: what you found, what was flaky, and what you proved.

64
00:02:52,549 --> 00:02:57,648
Go to the lab folder.

65
00:02:59,198 --> 00:03:01,096
Look around.

66
00:03:01,646 --> 00:03:02,517
The app code,

67
00:03:02,517 --> 00:03:03,387
shop.py.

68
00:03:03,387 --> 00:03:04,592
A folder of tests.

69
00:03:04,592 --> 00:03:05,395
A task file.

70
00:03:05,395 --> 00:03:06,467
And a CI script,

71
00:03:06,467 --> 00:03:08,140
which does not exist yet,

72
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,881
because you will write it.

73
00:03:10,431 --> 00:03:15,914
Mission one: run the tests.

74
00:03:16,464 --> 00:03:17,194
One failed.

75
00:03:17,194 --> 00:03:18,656
A cart with two lines,

76
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:19,851
ten dollars twice,

77
00:03:19,851 --> 00:03:21,313
and five dollars once,

78
00:03:21,313 --> 00:03:23,505
should total twenty-five dollars.

79
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:24,966
The code says fifteen.

80
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:26,162
The test is right.

81
00:03:26,162 --> 00:03:28,154
The code ignores the quantity.

82
00:03:28,704 --> 00:03:36,619
Fix the code.

83
00:03:37,169 --> 00:03:39,750
Run again.

84
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,659
Three passed. But there is something wrong with one of them.

85
00:03:44,209 --> 00:03:49,542
Mission two: the clock.

86
00:03:50,092 --> 00:03:52,178
The test calls is weekend sale,

87
00:03:52,178 --> 00:03:53,053
with no date.

88
00:03:53,053 --> 00:03:54,869
So it reads the real clock.

89
00:03:54,869 --> 00:03:55,946
Today it passes.

90
00:03:55,946 --> 00:03:56,888
On a Saturday,

91
00:03:56,888 --> 00:03:57,493
it fails,

92
00:03:57,493 --> 00:03:58,839
with no code change.

93
00:03:59,389 --> 00:04:05,106
Mission three: coverage.

94
00:04:05,656 --> 00:04:06,863
Fifty-nine percent.

95
00:04:06,863 --> 00:04:11,500
The column on the right lists the lines nobody tests: the unknown coupon,

96
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:12,643
the shipping rule,

97
00:04:12,643 --> 00:04:14,104
and the whole checkout.

98
00:04:14,654 --> 00:04:25,961
Rewrite the tests.

99
00:04:41,011 --> 00:04:45,363
The error is checked with pytest raises. That covers the unknown coupon.

100
00:04:45,913 --> 00:04:50,756
Add the rest.

101
00:05:18,506 --> 00:05:19,071
Saturday,

102
00:05:19,071 --> 00:05:19,763
and Friday,

103
00:05:19,763 --> 00:05:20,454
both fixed.

104
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:21,334
Five thousand,

105
00:05:21,334 --> 00:05:24,038
and four thousand nine hundred ninety-nine.

106
00:05:24,038 --> 00:05:25,106
And one checkout,

107
00:05:25,106 --> 00:05:26,426
from start to finish.

108
00:05:26,426 --> 00:05:27,935
Nothing reads the clock.

109
00:05:28,485 --> 00:05:30,320
Run with coverage.

110
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:35,354
Five passed.

111
00:05:35,354 --> 00:05:37,512
And the coverage is above ninety.

112
00:05:37,512 --> 00:05:38,950
Only one line is left,

113
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:41,369
the weekend discount inside checkout,

114
00:05:41,369 --> 00:05:42,676
and that is allowed.

115
00:05:43,226 --> 00:05:47,600
Mission four: the gate.

116
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:58,821
Three rules in three lines.

117
00:05:58,821 --> 00:06:01,838
Run the tests with a coverage floor of ninety.

118
00:06:01,838 --> 00:06:03,543
Fail if a secret is found.

119
00:06:03,543 --> 00:06:04,461
Anything else,

120
00:06:04,461 --> 00:06:04,986
success.

121
00:06:05,536 --> 00:06:09,056
Run the gate.

122
00:06:09,606 --> 00:06:11,696
Exit zero. The gate is open.

123
00:06:12,246 --> 00:06:15,617
Plant a secret.

124
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:17,276
Run the gate.

125
00:06:20,726 --> 00:06:24,801
Exit one. The gate is closed. A secret never reaches production.

126
00:06:25,351 --> 00:06:26,418
Remove it.

127
00:06:27,768 --> 00:06:32,888
Mission five: the report.

128
00:06:35,438 --> 00:06:38,723
Look at it.

129
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:39,767
The bug,

130
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:40,754
the flaky cause,

131
00:06:40,754 --> 00:06:41,557
the coverage,

132
00:06:41,557 --> 00:06:43,038
and the number of tests.

133
00:06:43,038 --> 00:06:45,507
A teammate can read this in ten seconds,

134
00:06:45,507 --> 00:06:46,804
and check every line.

135
00:06:47,354 --> 00:06:49,722
Run the judge.

136
00:06:50,272 --> 00:06:51,596
Six checks: the fix,

137
00:06:51,596 --> 00:06:52,722
a reliable suite,

138
00:06:52,722 --> 00:06:53,583
the coverage,

139
00:06:53,583 --> 00:06:55,305
three planted bugs caught,

140
00:06:55,305 --> 00:06:55,901
the gate,

141
00:06:55,901 --> 00:06:56,894
and the report.

142
00:06:56,894 --> 00:06:57,888
Six out of six.

143
00:06:58,438 --> 00:07:00,400
Clean up.

144
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:02,998
Removed. Nothing is left behind.

145
00:07:04,548 --> 00:07:08,559
Your mastery task. The same scenario, on your own machine, without me.

146
00:07:09,109 --> 00:07:09,996
Find the bug,

147
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:11,157
and fix the code.

148
00:07:11,157 --> 00:07:12,454
Fix the flaky test,

149
00:07:12,454 --> 00:07:13,683
with a fixed date.

150
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:14,297
No clock,

151
00:07:14,297 --> 00:07:14,980
no random,

152
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:15,594
no sleep.

153
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:17,039
Cover the code,

154
00:07:17,039 --> 00:07:18,592
to ninety percent or more,

155
00:07:18,592 --> 00:07:19,726
and test the edges.

156
00:07:19,726 --> 00:07:23,248
Your tests must catch the three bugs that the judge plants.

157
00:07:23,798 --> 00:07:24,974
Write the CI gate.

158
00:07:24,974 --> 00:07:26,542
It must pass when clean.

159
00:07:26,542 --> 00:07:27,979
It must fail on a bug,

160
00:07:27,979 --> 00:07:29,025
on low coverage,

161
00:07:29,025 --> 00:07:30,070
and on a secret.

162
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:33,948
Write the four line report. Then lab check, and lab down.

163
00:07:35,998 --> 00:07:38,897
Here is where to find everything for the whole domain.

164
00:07:38,897 --> 00:07:40,024
Pause on this screen,

165
00:07:40,024 --> 00:07:40,990
and write it down.

166
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:43,250
The labs live on GitHub,

167
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:44,413
at it-waves

168
00:07:44,413 --> 00:07:45,986
/devops-ai,

169
00:07:45,986 --> 00:07:47,491
in the folder academy,

170
00:07:47,491 --> 00:07:48,175
/lab.

171
00:07:48,725 --> 00:07:52,586
This lesson has two files: lab144.sh,

172
00:07:52,586 --> 00:07:55,231
and shortcuts144.sh.

173
00:07:55,781 --> 00:07:56,642
Install it,

174
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:59,382
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

175
00:07:59,382 --> 00:08:01,182
dash m seven five five,

176
00:08:01,182 --> 00:08:03,296
lab144.sh,

177
00:08:03,296 --> 00:08:04,548
into /usr

178
00:08:04,548 --> 00:08:05,487
/local

179
00:08:05,487 --> 00:08:06,427
/sbin.

180
00:08:06,977 --> 00:08:11,630
Load the short names with: source shortcuts144.sh.

181
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:12,811
You get two: lab,

182
00:08:12,811 --> 00:08:13,227
and T.

183
00:08:13,777 --> 00:08:15,496
You need python three,

184
00:08:15,496 --> 00:08:16,199
pytest,

185
00:08:16,199 --> 00:08:17,527
and pytest-cov.

186
00:08:17,527 --> 00:08:20,496
On Debian or Ubuntu: sudo apt install,

187
00:08:20,496 --> 00:08:21,043
dash Y,

188
00:08:21,043 --> 00:08:22,762
python three pytest,

189
00:08:22,762 --> 00:08:25,105
and python three pytest-cov.

190
00:08:25,655 --> 00:08:27,668
Lab up prepares the project.

191
00:08:27,668 --> 00:08:29,609
Lab check judges your work.

192
00:08:29,609 --> 00:08:31,334
Lab down removes it all.

193
00:08:31,334 --> 00:08:33,419
It uses the folder /opt

194
00:08:33,419 --> 00:08:35,216
/lab144.

195
00:08:35,216 --> 00:08:37,517
Only run it on your own machine.

196
00:08:38,067 --> 00:08:40,584
The earlier lessons each have their own lab,

197
00:08:40,584 --> 00:08:41,843
with the same pattern.

198
00:08:41,843 --> 00:08:44,360
Redo any of them whenever you need practice.

199
00:08:46,410 --> 00:08:48,479
Pass or fail. You need all six.

200
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:52,059
One: the bug is fixed, and totals count the quantity.

201
00:08:52,609 --> 00:08:57,857
Two: the suite is reliable: twelve runs, three time zones, and no clock or random.

202
00:08:58,407 --> 00:09:02,012
Three: coverage of shop.py is ninety percent or more.

203
00:09:02,562 --> 00:09:04,973
Four: your tests catch three planted bugs.

204
00:09:05,523 --> 00:09:10,835
Five: the CI gate passes when clean, and fails on a bug, low coverage, and a secret.

205
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:13,966
Six: the report has the four true values.

206
00:09:14,516 --> 00:09:15,817
To pass, all six.

207
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:19,638
Your turn, on your own machine.

208
00:09:20,188 --> 00:09:23,153
One: lab up. Run the tests, and fix the one bug.

209
00:09:23,703 --> 00:09:26,306
Two: fix the flaky test, with a fixed date.

210
00:09:26,856 --> 00:09:29,949
Three: cover the code. Test the edges, and the error.

211
00:09:30,499 --> 00:09:34,360
Four: write the gate, and try to break it, with a bug, and with a secret.

212
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:39,753
Five: write the report. Then lab check, until six out of six. Then lab down.

213
00:09:40,303 --> 00:09:42,138
Pause the video, and begin now.

214
00:09:57,688 --> 00:09:58,563
Quick check.

215
00:09:59,113 --> 00:10:02,569
Why must a test pass a fixed date, instead of reading the clock?

216
00:10:03,119 --> 00:10:06,105
Why can coverage be high, and the tests still be weak?

217
00:10:06,655 --> 00:10:09,535
What must a CI gate do, and when must it say no?

218
00:10:10,085 --> 00:10:11,451
What does your report prove?

219
00:10:12,001 --> 00:10:15,199
Objectives covered: all eight of MC15,

220
00:10:15,199 --> 00:10:16,975
software testing and Q A.

221
00:10:16,975 --> 00:10:19,818
Mastery evidence: a verifiable scenario,

222
00:10:19,818 --> 00:10:20,742
with results,

223
00:10:20,742 --> 00:10:21,879
troubleshooting,

224
00:10:21,879 --> 00:10:22,731
and cleanup.

225
00:10:23,281 --> 00:10:25,351
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

226
00:10:35,901 --> 00:10:39,527
Congratulations: the software testing domain is complete.

227
00:10:40,077 --> 00:10:44,259
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss the next domain.
